"Le won, les prix et la monnaie à rendre": "The won, prices and change",
"La monnaie sud-coréenne est le won : 원, symbole ₩, code KRW. Les prix utilisent les nombres sino-coréens. 1 000 = 천, 5 000 = 오천, 10 000 = 만, 50 000 = 오만. Les billets actuels ont ces quatre valeurs. Pour les pièces, retiens notamment 10, 50, 100 et 500 wons. Un prix de 12 500 wons se décompose en 만 (10 000) + 이천 (2 000) + 오백 (500) + 원. Attention : 100 000 = 십만 et 1 000 000 = 백만. On regroupe autour de 만 (10 000), pas uniquement par milliers.": "The South Korean currency is the won: 원, symbol ₩, code KRW. Prices use Sino-Korean numbers. 1,000 = 천, 5,000 = 오천, 10,000 = 만, 50,000 = 오만. Current banknotes have these four values. For coins, remember in particular 10, 50, 100 and 500 won. A price of 12,500 won breaks down into 만 (10,000) + 이천 (2,000) + 오백 (500) + 원. Careful: 100,000 = 십만 and 1,000,000 = 백만. Numbers are grouped around 만 (10,000), not only by thousands.",
"이거 = ceci ; 얼마예요? = combien ça coûte ? → C’est 12 500 wons.": "이거 = this; 얼마예요? = how much is it? → It’s 12,500 won.",
"거스름돈 = monnaie rendue ; 은 = thème ; 이천오백 원 = 2 500 wons. Si tu paies 10 000 pour un prix de 7 500, on te rend 2 500.": "거스름돈 = change; 은 = topic; 이천오백 원 = 2,500 won. If you pay 10,000 for a price of 7,500, you get 2,500 back.",
"카드로 = par carte ; 결제할게요 = je vais payer. → Je vais payer par carte.": "카드로 = by card; 결제할게요 = I’ll pay. → I’ll pay by card.",
"12 500 wons ?": "12,500 won?",
"Un billet de 50 000 wons se lit…": "A 50,000-won note is read…",
"100 000 wons ?": "100,000 won?",
"Tu paies 10 000 pour 7 500. On rend…": "You pay 10,000 for 7,500. You get back…",
"Quelle question demande le prix ?": "Which question asks for the price?",
