"Dates, téléphone et quantités": "Dates, phone numbers and quantities",
"Les dates se lisent en sino-coréen : année + 년, mois + 월, jour + 일. Juin = 유월 et octobre = 시월 sont deux exceptions. Dans un téléphone, lis les chiffres un par un et utilise 공 pour zéro. Pour compter des objets, utilise souvent un nombre natif suivi du compteur adapté : 개 (objets), 잔 (tasses), 명 (personnes), 권 (livres). La durée en jours se travaille à part : 하루 = un jour, 이틀 = deux jours.": "Dates are read in Sino-Korean: year + 년, month + 월, day + 일. June = 유월 and October = 시월 are two exceptions. In a phone number, read the digits one by one and use 공 for zero. To count objects, you often use a native number followed by the right counter: 개 (objects), 잔 (cups), 명 (people), 권 (books). Durations in days are learnt separately: 하루 = one day, 이틀 = two days.",
"유월 = juin ; 십오 일 = le 15. → C’est le 15 juin.": "유월 = June; 십오 일 = the 15th. → It’s 15 June.",
"책 = livres ; 세 = trois ; 권 = compteur de livres ; 주세요 = donnez-moi s’il vous plaît.": "책 = books; 세 = three; 권 = counter for books; 주세요 = please give me.",
"커피 = café ; 두 = deux ; 잔 = tasses ; 주세요 = s’il vous plaît.": "커피 = coffee; 두 = two; 잔 = cups; 주세요 = please.",
